 `applyPatch(document, patch)` applies an [RFC 6902 JSON Patch](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6902)
 array and returns the resulting JSON value. It supports `add`, `remove`, `replace`, `move`, `copy` and
-`test`. The input document is left unchanged; an invalid patch or failed operation throws an error.
+`test`. Operations run in order on a copy of the input. A failed operation throws and returns no
+partial result; the input remains unchanged. The document and patch must contain valid JSON values.
+Operation-specific required fields and JSON Pointers are validated, while unrecognized operation
+members are ignored as required by RFC 6902. A `test` compares JSON values structurally, including
+objects whose members appear in a different order.
